/**
 * Finds the optimal position to wrap a line of text within a specified width, starting from a given position.
 * This method prioritizes explicit line breaks (newline, tab) within the allowed width.
 * If no explicit break is found, it attempts to find a natural word break (whitespace) by searching backward
 * from the maximum allowed wrap position. If a word is longer than the specified width, it will
 * "chop" the word at the maximum allowed wrap position and then search forward for the next whitespace
 * to determine the actual wrap point.
 *
 * @param text The complete string to be wrapped. Must not be null.
 * @param width The maximum desired width for the current line segment. Must be positive.
 * @param startPos The starting index in the text from which to begin searching for a wrap point.
 *                 Must be non-negative and less than or equal to the text's length.
 * @return The index in the text where the current line segment should end (i.e., the character at this index
 *         will be the first character of the next line segment).
 *         If an explicit newline or tab character is found, the returned position is *after* that character.
 *         Returns -1 if no further wrap point is needed (the remaining text fits within the width,
 *         or no suitable wrap point is found until the end of the string).
 * @throws IllegalArgumentException if text is null, width is non-positive, or startPos is out of bounds.
 */

